"Beneath the physical world lies the arcanic sea, a layer of arcana few arcanists ever enter."
"In the arcanic sea the body's senses fail; arcanic sense shows a surface and depths below."
"Diving deeper in the sea taps more potent energies; complexity lives at depth."
"In the sea minds can speak to one another; thoughts and feelings leak unless sealed."
"Each person has a thread linking mind and body in the sea; it can guide one back."
"In the sea one cannot read glyphs and must work by intuition."
"Beyond the arcanic sea lies oblivion, a non-space where only time, emotion and thought hold."
"The veil is the limit of perception; the physical world itself is part of the veil."
"To pierce the veil one drops every sense-based frame; pain there comes from clinging to flesh."
"In oblivion emotions turn literal and senses cross; one must think softly or be torn apart."
"Arcanists who can perceive the higher layers are called sighted."
"A flare reaches into higher dimensions; the body is but branches of a much larger tree."
"Wysana are creations of pure arcana made by one particular frameshift."
"A wysana is framed as an intelligent construct, with the emotional core of a friend."
"Without that emotional core a construct is unstable and lasts only while the will holds it."
"A wysana needs a physical anchor, has no flare, and dwells mostly within oblivion."
"Making a wysana needs sequences scribed in a prepared space plus several artefacts."
"Making a stable wysana is teachable, no harder than other advanced arcanophany."
"The Fateweavers suppress wysana lore, as it would let people do advanced work unaided."
"The Demiurge may keep a few wysana; some Nightwatchers and scattered others have them too."
"The Academy's library cafe is run by a wysana that knows each patron's order."
"A person's arcanic self is truly the auric-ambient-flare, and it is best framed as a light."
"A flare's brightness can be turned up; radiated as warm light, it can hold back an augera."
"Flares have aspects, named in three linked words, such as warm-skilful-bridge."
"The surfaced aspects are the face; deeper aspects hold bonds, learning and primal traits."
"Trauma can surface deeper aspects, and damage to a flare can change its face name."
"The augera speak in hyphenated bundles of concepts; understanding them can overwhelm."
"Knowledge binds: to understand a thing fully reshapes one's flare, so the knower changes."
"Knowing a thing gives power over it, and it over you; awareness tightens prophetic links."
"Ensorcelment is the weaponising of how flares work, and it can pass binding knowledge."
"The shape of knowing, \"the shadow of thought\", is a glyph-complex naming mental poses."
"Knowledge can pass flare to flare as a knot that the recipient unravels and absorbs."
"Such knowledge-passing is an invitation, not a compulsion, though it feels like ensorcelment."
"The same knowledge sits in a different shape in every flare."
"Knowledge-passing is a building block of Fateweaver craft and of the great memory wipe."
"Flare-hiding dips into oblivion and twists a flare there, while the mind stays behind."
"Hidden people cannot see their own flares and stay open to sight and area attacks."
"A sharp thaumaturgist can still find the body of someone whose flare is hidden."
"Going high enough in the stream's upper reaches also hides the flow of arcana."
"Phasing lifts oneself, by one's oblivion parts, out of the plane an attack acts on."
"Shields do not come along when one phases; phasing sequences themselves come later."
"Phase-movement: conjure a sphere of arcana as a target and will oneself to it."
"The Demiurge's \"teleport\" is phasing done by folding oblivion; true teleportation isn't real."
"Will-only work succeeds because arcana forms a brief construct shaped to the caster's intent."
"Glyphs seem a language between flares and the augera, who wield arcana on the user's behalf."
"Reeves's ensorcelment frames arcana as light, which is why it can be partly blocked."
"All arcanophany, every glyph and artefact, rests on the structure the augera network provides."
"Free the augera and the Special Set may break, buildings fall and artefacts explode."
"Other nations have some arcanophany but, as far as is known, no augera."
"The lay account of overdraw is incomplete; the augera tie it to their will-curse-test."
"The augera hold a recovery sequence from the Fateweavers' dawn that heals near any wound."
"A rare few, the Chosen One among them, can mind-speak with no gestalt at all."
